CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^\*\* 0 of \d+ failed
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^bad reference initializer$
^warning: ignoring
^.*FAILURE$
--
[temp.deduct.conv]/2 + /4 + [over.match.ref]: template
conversion-operator deduction for reference targets.  When the
parameter's return type is a reference, /2 strips it; when the
destination is a reference, /4 strips it.  Deduction then runs on
the unwrapped types.  After instantiation the resulting reference
must bind directly to the source object (verified by mutating
through the reference and observing the change in the source).
